verseen by dioikites or oikonomos.<br>The Seleucid Empire did have full time bureaucrats, and this system in the Greco-Bactrians also seems to have existed. It is therefore inferred that some element of this system was preserved.<br>1. King<br>2. Topio overseen by the dioikites<i>(Note that under the Seleucids the title Dioketes denoted the individuals responsible for finances, royal land, revenue and expenditure and whom possibly also supervised royal mints and registry offices.)</i><br>3. EpistatesNote: if it translates directly as the Ancient Greek term, an overseer or superintendent.<br>4. Scribes <i>inferred</i><br><br>5. Panchayat (council of elders.) <br>'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 1014, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 861})
