, and there were half a dozen of these in each bailliage.<br>prévot farmed the revenues of the royal domain and rendered justice at a local level.<br>a "prevote" was a military region used in the raising of armed forces (end 12th century)<br>5. Leader of a parishCities could be divided into parishes <br>'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 1413, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 1309})
