he minor sub-sections (wilaya) of the entire region (niyaba). <br>often the wali al-wulat also doubled as the shadd or mushidd al-dawawin "whose duty it was to check and observe the collection of the Sultans\' dues and taxes from state estates."<br>5<small>syria</small> Wali, officer of a small town"The wali was a police officer in charge of keeping law and order in town. His rank: Amir of Ten. One should not confuse him with wali al-wulat, who was higher in authority and rank, being an Amir of Forty, and who was responsible for the minor sub-sections (wilaya) of the entire region (niyaba). <br>6<small>syria</small> Village head.<br>'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 1520, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 1405})
