pose (e.g. as a list of counted goods). Moreover, the scrutinized analysis of seals and sealings from sites such as Tepe Gawra, Niniveh proved that the administrative system became more centralized starting from the Middle Uruk Period and focused on \'control of local movements and storage of goods\'.  Moreover, some researchers emphasize that elaborated settlement hierarchy must equal elaborated administrative level: ,influential idea was that at least three tiers of settlement within one settlement system represented an underlying administrative structure with at least three levels of hierarchy.'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 908, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 762})
